    "title": "Incredible 40-million-year-old discovery of 'thunder beast' fossils - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julia Musto ,\n1 days ago The plaster jacket surrounding the bones City of Oceanside - Government/Facebook Infrastructure workers in Oceanside , California, uncovered 40-to-45-million-year-old fossilized bones of an ancient hoofed mammal. Paleontologist Dr. Joseph El Adli discovered the fossils , which include several ribs and a femur, during routine project monitoring. Experts believe the remains belong to either an elephant -sized brontothere or an amynodont, a hornless, hippo-shaped swamp rhino . The fossils were excavated 12 feet deep within the Santiago Formation, a rock layer dating back to the Eocene epoch. The bones were transported in a plaster jacket to a climate-controlled laboratory for cleaning, research, and eventual museum placement. IN FULL\nCalifornia workers discover 40-million-year-old animal bones at construction site",
